# Farm OS design guardrails (binding)

Authoritative presentation source: `docs/ux/animal-farm-visual-lock/`. The older design-system spec is operational guidance only where compatible.
Read the relevant section before writing or reviewing UI code. These are CI-enforced laws, not suggestions.

## Visual authority

- The current visual authority is the Animal Farm visual-lock pack. External repos (nowinandroid, compose-samples, etc.) are ENGINEERING references only - never consult them for layout, spacing, colour or component choice.
- Every screen uses the assigned Animal Farm PAGE-PATTERNS recipe after field/action/permission review. Old named patterns do not override A management or D+C worker. New layouts require reviewed design contracts.

## Hard bans (CI fails these)

- Gradients anywhere in feature UI (`Brush.linearGradient/radialGradient`)
- Emoji in UI copy, empty states or string resources
- Raw `Color(0x...)`, raw `dp/sp` outside approved scales, non-Inter fonts, ad-hoc `TextStyle(...)` outside `:core-design/theme`
- Material 2 APIs; direct `MaterialTheme.colorScheme/typography` usage outside `:core-design`
- Placeholder content in committed code/tests: Lorem, Item 1, Test, Sample, John Doe, foo
- Decorative animation libraries (Lottie, confetti, particles) without an accepted EDR

## Required states and fixtures

- Every interactive surface defines all five states: idle, loading, empty, error, disabled. Use the shared loadable-state wrapper; never render bare lists.
- All previews/screenshots/demo data use the named fixtures (Nala goat record, Cage B KudBat wave, August money records) from the fixtures module.

## Copy voice

- Verb-first buttons, sentence case, terse. Numbers as figures. Species vocabulary exact (kidding=goat, kindling=rabbit). No exclamation marks, no marketing tone, no "simply/easily/just".
- Errors state what happened AND the fix, plus data-safety reassurance for sync failures.

## Process (non-negotiable)

1. Gallery-first: new screens appear in the Gallery debug entry with fixtures BEFORE integration PRs; owner pixel-approval precedes implementation.
2. Screenshot evidence: Roborazzi/Paparazzi goldens (light/dark/outdoor x font-scale 1.0/1.3/2.0) updated in the same PR; CI diffs block merge.
3. Tests green != UI done. Phase gates require owner visual sign-off of the gallery diff and a clean outdoor sunlight walk for release trains.
4. Token-lint violations trend per module; rising aesthetic debt freezes new feature UI in that module until zero.

When blocked on a visual decision not covered by the spec: stop, cite the pattern code you tried to apply, and ask - do not improvise from memory or repos.
